#X text 152 542 Here we recuperate the pointer using a named [vpointer] and use [get] to see the values of all 5 fields. Changing the values in the number boxes sends messages ti [set] objects that change the values \, as you can see in the window.;
#X text 211 623 <-- get pointer to next scalar;
#X text 353 652 <-- rewind to first scalar;
#X text 34 841 In this example the "data03" window is flipped so that y grows upward \, not downward: this was done using the preferences dialog for the window \, setting y units per pixel to 1 instead of its default -1 . When you resize the window the objects now stick to the bottom margin instead of the top one. This is how scalars are most often displayed., f 84;
#X text 538 940 Updated for version 0.57;
#N canvas 503 200 512 309 struct03 0;
#X text 44 53 five numeric ("float") fields;
#X text 54 252 This also allows you to click on the drawn number and drag or type to change the color parameter.;
